1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,000
Building Kubernetes from the ground up — no managed service.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Three EC2 instances on Amazon Linux 2023: one control plane, two workers.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
The real thing: all three instances running in my AWS account.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
containerd with systemd cgroups, kernel networking prep, kubeadm v1.37.2.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,000
kubeadm init, kubeadm join, and Flannel for Pod networking. All three nodes Ready.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,500
An Nginx Deployment with two replicas…

7
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:38,000
…and the scheduler placed one Pod on each worker. 2/2 Available.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
A NodePort Service on port 32170 routes traffic to both Pods.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Next step: verify external browser access through the NodePort.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Project 01: Self-Managed Kubernetes on AWS EC2.
